    "https://hr.umn.edu/jobs/Find-Job/Executive-Searches/Executive-Director-Admissions-UMN-Duluth": {
      "title": "Executive Director of Admissions – UMN Duluth",
      "description": "Executive Director of Admissions – UMN Duluth | University of Minnesota Office of Human Resources Skip to main content Go to the University of Minnesota Twin Cities home page One Stop MyU : For Students, Faculty, and Staff Search Office of Human Resources Jobs Why the UMN Benefits at UMN Relocation Assistance Find a Job Search UMN Jobs UMN Student Jobs Featured Positions U Services Positions Veterinary Technician Positions Executive Searches Associate Chancellor - Crookston Executive Director of Admissions – UMN Duluth Executive Medical Director - Boynton Health Vice Chancellor for Enrollment Management - UMN Morris Applicant Support Using the Job Application System Application and Interview Guidance UMN Graduate Assistant Job Guidance UMN Undergraduate Student Job Guidance Veteran Employment Guidance Contact Breadcrumb Home Find a Job Executive Searches Executive Director of Admissions – UMN Duluth Executive Director of Admissions – UMN Duluth The Executive Director of Admissions serves as the University’s senior admissions leader, providing strategic leadership for the admissions enterprise. Reporting to the Vice Chancellor for Strategic Enrollment Management, the Executive Director leads first-year, transfer, and international recruitment while providing executive oversight for admissions strategy, operations, partnerships, and organizational effectiveness. Working collaboratively with academic and administrative leaders across the university, the Executive Director develops and implements recruitment strategies, strengthens the prospective student experience, advances data-informed decision-making, fosters innovation across the admissions enterprise, and cultivates a high-performing admissions organization that advances institutional enrollment priorities. In collaboration with graduate education and program leadership, this position serves as a strategic thought partner by identifying opportunities to strengthen graduate recruitment strategies and build organizational capacity for future enrollment growth. Contact Contact Angie Windnagel at [email protected] with any questions about the position or location. Learn more about this role at the University Your browser does not support iframes, but you can visit Five Strong Campuses. One Strong State. The University of Minnesota System is one of the most comprehensive in the nation, with offerings to meet the interests of every student and the changing needs of our society. We're proud of our land-grant mission of world-class education, groundbreaking research, and our commitment to partnering with communities in our drive to serve Minnesota. Learn more about the University of Minnesota System. Learn more about our world-class benefits Learn More Expand all Learn More + About UMN Duluth The University of Minnesota Duluth (UMD) is a student-centered medium-sized public research university integrating liberal education, public engagement, and sustainability. Overlooking Lake Superior, UMD provides professional programs, hands-on discovery, and robust campus life within the vibrant port city of Duluth. Learn more about UMN Duluth + Responsibilities Admissions Strategy and Planning (20%) Lead the development and implementation of admissions and recruitment strategies aligned with institutional enrollment priorities Translate Strategic Enrollment Management priorities into actionable recruitment plans and measurable outcomes. Advise university leadership on enrollment trends, demographic shifts, market conditions, recruitment performance, and competitor activity to inform institutional decision-making Facilitate the development, communication, and assessment of undergraduate enrollment targets in partnership with academic leadership and campus stakeholders Collaborate with the Office of Institutional Research, the budget & analysis office, and external partners to develop enrollment projections, scenario modeling, tuition revenue analysis, and long-range enrollment planning Lead enrollment analysis related to recruitment performance, student behavior, market trends, and enrollment funnel outcomes to support strategic planning and financial sustainability Contribute to institutional discussions related to enrollment strategy, academic planning, resource allocation, and long-term university priorities Recruitment and Student Conversion (20%) Lead recruitment strategy for first-year, transfer, and international student populations through territory management, market expansion, lead generation, and outreach initiatives Develop strategies that strengthen application generation, student conversion, yield, and enrollment outcomes Partner with Enrollment Marketing and Communications to align recruitment strategy, communications, market positioning, and prospective student engagement Collaborate with Financial Aid and Scholarships to inform financial aid leveraging and optimization strategies in consultation with the Vice Chancellor for Strategic Enrollment Management and the budget & analysis office Coordinate cross-functional recruitment efforts with strategic enrollment management, academic, student life, and other campus partners to strengthen enrollment outcomes and the prospective student experience Provide strategic oversight of international recruitment in partnership with International Programs and Services, and collaborate with graduate and professional programs to strengthen recruitment strategies and advance enrollment growth across student populations Partner with University Marketing and Public Relations to ensure alignment between recruitment strategy, institutional messaging, and brand positioning Partnerships and Pathways (20%) Develop and strengthen partnerships with school districts, community colleges, community organizations, and other external partners to support recruitment, educational access, and enrollment goals Advance transfer pathways, articulation agreements, and other partnership models that strengthen long-term enrollment opportunities Provide strategic leadership for the integration of Postsecondary Enrollment Options (PSEO), College in the Schools, and related outreach initiatives as organizational responsibilities evolve Align campus outreach, youth engagement, and pathway initiatives with institutional enrollment priorities to strengthen long-term recruitment pipelines and institutional awareness Partner with academic leadership to align recruitment strategies with workforce needs, evolving student interests, academic program priorities, and future program development Enterprise Modernization and Operational Excellence (20%) Provide strategic leadership for undergraduate admissions operations, including recruitment operations, application processing, analysis, territory management, and visit programs Lead modernization of admissions systems, operational processes, policies, communication strategies, and organizational workflows to improve effectiveness and scalability Ensure effective use of customer relationship management (CRM) systems, enrollment technologies, data infrastructure, and performance metrics to support strategic decision-making and continuous improvement Utilize data analysis and enrollment insights to evaluate recruitment effectiveness, identify opportunities, and improve organizational performance across the enrollment funnel Lead process improvement initiatives and evaluate emerging technologies, including artificial intelligence, to strengthen recruitment strategy, operational effectiveness, and the prospective student experience Manage budgets, staffing models, and resource allocation to support organizational priorities and enrollment outcomes Organizational Leadership and Talent Development (10%) Provide strategic leadership and organizational direction across the admissions enterprise Recruit, develop, coach, and retain a high-performing admissions team while fostering collaboration, accountability, innovation, and continuous improvement Establish a distributed leadership model with clear ownership and decision-making across functional areas Assess organizational structure and recommend improvements that enhance effectiveness, scalability, succession planning, and future organizational capacity Community and External Engagement (10%) Represent the university in regional, state, and national organizations, professional associations, and strategic partnerships Serve as a spokesperson for admissions, enrollment, and recruitment initiatives through media interviews, public communications, and community engagement Represent the university in public discussions related to admissions strategy, student access, and institutional enrollment growth Strengthen relationships with school counselors, school and district leaders, employers, alumni, civic leaders, community organizations, and educational partners to advance the university's visibility, recruitment efforts, and strategic partnerships Other Duties Perform other duties as assigned in support of the mission, goals, and strategic priorities of the unit, division, and university. + Qualifications Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree plus at least 12 years of relevant experience, or master's degree plus at least 10 years of relevant experience Progressive leadership experience in admissions, enrollment management, recruitment, student services, or related higher education functions Experience leading strategic initiatives, operational planning, or organizational projects within a complex organization Experience leading professional staff, teams, or cross functional initiatives. Strong communication, presentation, and relationship building skills Preferred Qualifications Master's degree in higher education, business, public administration/policy, or a related field Experience serving as the chief admissions officer, Director of Admissions, or in an equivalent senior leadership role leading undergraduate admissions Experience leading enrollment growth initiatives and improving net tuition revenue outcomes Experience developing enrollment projections, scenario modeling, or long range enrollment planning in collaboration with institutional partners Experience with international recruitment strategy and global enrollment initiatives Experience developing strategies that strengthen application generation, student conversion, yield, and enrollment outcomes Experience facilitating undergraduate enrollment target development in partnership with academic leadership and campus stakeholders Experience partnering with graduate and professional program leaders to support recruitment strategy or enrollment growth Experience overseeing dual enrollment, College in the Schools/PSEO, or other early pipeline initiatives Experience developing strategic partnerships with employers, community organizations, or regional partners Experience leading organizational modernization, process improvement, change management, or implementation of data informed technologies, including CRM systems and AI supported tools, to improve organizational effectiveness and strategic decision making Experience representing an institution through public presentations, media interactions, or external partnership settings + Salary, Benefits, and Other Details Starting salary range : $106,000–$130,000 annually Benefits : As a Professional and Administrative (P&A) employee, you’ll enjoy a comprehensive benefits package with low-cost health coverage, professional development opportunities, and retirement plan with 10% employer contribution. (See our benefits page for more information.) + Applications and Nominations Please submit both a cover letter and a resume (or CV). Apply here Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For best consideration, apply by September 21, 2026. Search Advisory Committee Adam Burke, Chair – Associate Vice Chancellor, Student Engagement and Wellbeing Anne Stevens – Dean, College of Arts, Humanities, and Social Sciences Erik Brown – Associate Vice Chancellor for Graduate Education and Research Chrissie Faupel – Director of International Affairs Susana Pelayo-Woodward – Director, Office of Diversity & Inclusion and Women's Resource and Action Center Marti Fasteland – Interim Director, Office of Admissions Jeremy Belanger – Director of Advising and Academic Services, Labovitz School of Business and Economics Bryan Martinez Mejia – UMD Student Body President Coming in as a candidate for a position through the executive search process, and having led executive searches in past organizations, my own bar was fairly high. Questions were handled professionally and compassionately. The candidate experience overall was positive and affirming, and I felt I was in good hands throughout. -Autumn Amadou-Blegen, SPHR, SHRM-SCP Associate Vice Chancellor of Human Resources 2026 Best Employers for Company Culture, Forbes 80% Would recommend to a friend, Glassdoor #4 Best States, U.S. News An Equal Opportunity Employer The University of Minnesota shall provide equal access to and opportunity in its programs, facilities, and employment without regard to race, color, creed, religion, national origin, gender, age, marital status, disability, public assistance status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression. Talent Acquisition | UMN Office of Human Resources Contact Email: [email protected] Student Employment Email: [email protected] Quick Links Find a Job Comprehensive Benefits Using the Application System This unit has systemwide responsibilities. Learn more about the University of Minnesota System . For Students, Faculty, and Staff One Stop MyU : For Students, Faculty, and Staff © 2026 Regents of the University of Minnesota . All rights reserved. The University of Minnesota is an equal opportunity educator and employer. Privacy Statement Report Web Accessibility Issues Benefits Benefits Enrollment and Changes Enrollment Overview Up